@startuml
title D-03 Normal Payment-to-Exit Flow with Fiscal Issuance

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor Parker
participant "WebPay / Channel" as Channel
participant "Central PMS" as Central
participant "Vendor PMS / HCP" as Vendor
participant "Payment Orchestrator" as Orchestrator
participant "Payment Provider" as Provider
participant "Resolved Site\nPOS Server" as POS
participant "Gate / Exit" as Gate

Parker -> Channel : open site-specific URL or payment channel
Channel -> Central : submit lookup / payment context
Central -> Central : resolve Site Group and Site
Central -> Vendor : request live session and fee
Vendor --> Central : session result and tariff computation
Central -> Central : create immutable TariffSnapshot
Central -> Orchestrator : initiate payment attempt
Orchestrator -> Provider : provider interaction
Provider --> Orchestrator : verified provider outcome
Orchestrator --> Central : report verified outcome
Central -> Central : record PaymentConfirmation
Central -> POS : request Sales Invoice issuance
POS --> Central : fiscal document identity / status
Central -> Central : record fiscal issuance reference
Central -> Gate : issue ExitAuthorization
Gate -> Gate : consume authorization
Central -> Vendor : payment acknowledgment where supported / required

note right of Central
Central PMS declares platform finality
and issues ExitAuthorization.
end note

note right of POS
Fiscal issuance succeeds before
ExitAuthorization is issued.
end note

@enduml
